AB  - Image registration is a prerequisite for remote sensing image fusion and classification, and registration accuracy affects the performance of these tasks. However, there are significant nonlinear radiation differences between optical and synthetic aperture radar (SAR) images and speckle noise in SAR, which limits the ability of pure convolutional neural networks (CNNs) to obtain modality-shared features. To solve these problems, this paper proposes a Multi-scale Frequency Attention Fusion Network for Optical and SAR image Registration (MFAF-OS-RegNet), which includes a Multi-scale Frequency Channel Attention Fusion (MFCAF) module and a Momentum Contrastive Learning (MCL) strategy. Firstly, we extract repeatable keypoints distributed on the edges and develop a novel MFCAF module to obtain modality-shared features. In the MFCAF module, multi-scale feature fusion is used to improve the positioning accuracy of matching points, and frequency channel attention is used to mine more favorable features. Secondly, we design a MCL strategy to reduce the interference of speckle noise in network training. The momentum teacher corrects handcrafted labels by learning the essential characteristics of the data for robust matching. Finally, we filter outliers and estimate transformation parameters based on the initial matching correspondence output by MFAF-OS-RegNet. Experimental results on a publicly available OS-dataset show that the proposed method outperforms other state-of-the-art methods.
