AB  - The extraction of buildings from remote sensing images has long been a prominent research topic in the field of remote sensing image analysis. In this study, we propose a novel approach for building extraction called ReUnet, which combines the residual network and U-net image segmentation network. This model utilizes the skeleton of U-net and the residual units of Resnet to address the issue of gradient diffusion during feature extraction in traditional U-net networks. The residual structure of ReUnet simplifies the training of deep networks and promotes information propagation. We evaluate our network using the LEVIR-CD dataset and compare it with three advanced deep learning-based methods for remote sensing building extraction, namely PSnet, U-net, and Resnet. The proposed method outperforms all compared methods in terms of its ability to accurately extract buildings. Overall, our results suggest that ReUnet is a promising approach for building extraction from remote sensing images.
