AB  - This project will study a digital surface elevation model (DSM) and an image semantic segmentation method based on multi-scale weight clustering. Taking the overall partitioning metric as a constraint, the weights are classified step by step using a multi-grid algebraic algorithm. An image processing method based on a single residual method is proposed for high-resolution remote sensing images. Row Height Information Mining with Convolutional Neural Networks is proposed. The method's accuracy can reach 92.33% through the test on the existing public database. The experimental results prove that the method extracts and fuses features of multiple levels and can obtain better semantic segmentation results.
